            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cedar Lake cook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a hit at our volunteer appreciation luncheon. I have already been asked to share the recipe. Instead of buying two half gallons of ice cream, I used a gallon of vanilla fudge swirl ice cream. I also added 4 cups milk. It was delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-06T00:06:28.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephanee P"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this! I didn't read the recipe before the morning I needed this so I made a quick \"cross my fingers\" alteration. I'll share for anyone else it might help. \n\nI boiled half the amount of water, added the sugar, coffee, and chocolate drink mix (although I didn't have any chocolate drink mix so I omitted this ingredient and my guests said that it was amazing without it). Stired to dissolve, then added the additional half of water to cool it. Then added my ice cream and cool whip. This recipe is seriously the best ever!",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-05T20:48:30.750Z"
          },
          {
